id: CustomFieldsBulkEditor
name: ᝯㄝₓ Custom Fields Bulk Editor
metadata:
  description: "View and bulk edit custom fields across a whole selection, or across the whole library. Select anything in an entity list (Scenes, Images, Galleries, Performers, Studios, Groups or Tags), open the \"...\" menu and pick \"Custom Fields...\" - or run the task in Settings - Tasks - Plugin Tasks to cover every entity of all seven types at once.\n\nThe dialog lists every custom field the entities in scope carry - one line per entity and field - with filters on the entity type, the field name, the entity itself and the value - each text filter matching either \"contains\" or \"omits\", and the value filter also offering \"is empty\", \"is true\" and \"is not true\". An [INFO] line names every custom field found, with a count. Click an entity to open it in a new tab, or a field name or value to copy it; copying a selection of lines gives plain text.\n\nOne field is written at a time, in one of four ways: Add sets it only where it is missing, Overwrite sets that one field everywhere, replacing the value already there and leaving the entity's other custom fields alone, Remove deletes it, and Rename moves the field itself to a new name, keeping every value - offered while everything in scope carries the same one field name. The write covers either everything in scope or only the lines the filters leave showing.\n\nNothing is written until you press Apply. Afterwards the list shows exactly what changed and Undo puts the previous values back, field by field, and stays offered while the dialog is open. Rescan re-reads without closing, and Copy log takes the counters, the messages and the whole listing as plain text.\n\nEvery custom field can also carry a description of its own, shown as a tooltip on the field name. The second task, \"Manage Custom Field Descriptions...\", scans the library, lists every field with what carries it, and keeps the descriptions in the description of one tag - so they live in the database, are covered by the database backup, and are the same in every browser.\n\nAn entity carrying the custom field named in the settings below is hidden from Stash's add/select dropdowns - the list you pick a tag, performer, studio, group, gallery or scene from while editing something else. It stays on its own list page, on the entities that already have it, and in the API.\n\nScene markers are not offered: they are the one selectable entity in Stash with no custom fields at all.\n\nRequires Stash 0.31.0 or newer."
